# TypeScript Inference

## Single source of truth

```typescript
// BAD — duplicated shape
interface User { id: string; name: string }

// GOOD — schema first, type inferred
const userSchema = z.object({ id: z.string(), name: z.string() })
type User = z.infer<typeof userSchema>
```

## Boundaries

- Validate `import.meta.env` in `@lib/env.ts`.
- Validate API responses in `@lib/api-client.ts` with Zod at the network boundary.
- Use `satisfies` for const maps; use `z.enum()` for string unions.

## Forbidden

- `any`, `enum`, `as SomeType`, non-null assertions (`!`).
- Interfaces that mirror an existing Zod schema.
